rents. Such informa-\ntion can then be used to determine the adequacy of the rate paid to\nproviders, as well as inform policy decisions to ensure childcare\nproviders remain stable. Therefore, this legislation moves one step\nforward in creating a more robust and better quality child care system.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\n2016-2017: S.1455(Avella)/A.290 (Jaffee)\n2015-16: A.9900-A (Jaffee)\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS FOR STATE AND LOCAL GOVERNMENTS:\n\nUndetermined.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
